      "notes": "All claims are properly tiered and the quotes entail the claims as stated. The \u00a3500 saving and 80,000\u2013100,000 poverty-lift figures are correctly marked projected and sourced to credible institutional sources (IFS/Resolution Foundation). The cost estimate is attributed to IFS and marked projected. The E27 claim about CPAG/National Food Strategy is advocacy-sourced but correctly used only to flag a definitional caveat rather than to drive the direction verdict, and it is labelled as 'analysts argue' (appropriately hedged). The direction 'improves' is well-supported: a targeted in-kind transfer to lower-income households is by construction redistributive downward, consistent with O14. The universal primary ambition is correctly discounted under the soft-verb rule. No tier blurring, no lever leakage, no party-blind issues, no false balance concern (the direction is not mixed/too-uncertain). No magnitude inflation \u2014 'moderate' is defensible given the projected poverty-lift is genuine but modest relative to total child poverty. One minor note: E2 is backed partly by cpag.org.uk (advocacy), but it is corroborated by commonslibrary.parliament.uk and other institutional sources in the same evidence unit, so it is not sole-advocacy. Overall the verdict is publication-ready."
